## This example specifically shows four things people always get wrong

| Done right | What happens if you screw up |
|---|---|
| Colors all use `var(--…)`, background and text paired | Hand-code hex → dark text on dark background / white on white, no error just invisible |
| **No call to `ready`** | Looking for `butlerUI.ready()` finds nothing —— the sandbox bridge sends that itself |
| Use `onInit` to get last session's state | Reading DOM at top level works too, but doesn't get state the host brought back |
| Handle `onPush` to show errors | setState over 64K **silently fails**, if you don't listen you never see it |
| Call with full name `hello_counter.say` | Declaration says `say`, but host always prefixes the package id. Short name won't resolve |

Also: call `resize` every time content changes, otherwise frame height is locked.

